MCPay is an open-source infrastructure that integrates on-chain payments into any Model Context Protocol (MCP) server using the x402 "Payment Required" protocol. This enables MCP clients, such as ChatGPT, to process pay-per-call requests without relying on static subscriptions or API keys. ([docs.mcpay.tech](https://docs.mcpay.tech/?utm_source=openai))

To integrate MCPay with ChatGPT, you can follow these steps:

1. **Open ChatGPT**: Navigate to the settings menu.
2. **Enable Developer Mode**: Under Advanced Settings, enable Developer Mode to access the Apps & Connectors section.
3. **Add MCP Server**: In the Apps & Connectors section, add a new MCP server with the following configuration:

   ```json
   {
     "mcpServers": {
       "mcpay": {
         "url": "https://mcpay.tech/mcp",
         "headers": {
           "Authorization": "Bearer <YOUR_API_KEY>"
         }
       }
     }
   }
   ```

   Replace `<YOUR_API_KEY>` with your actual API key from MCPay.

Once integrated, ChatGPT can autonomously handle on-chain payments for API calls, allowing for transparent and efficient pay-per-use transactions. ([docs.mcpay.tech](https://docs.mcpay.tech/?utm_source=openai))

